1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
Section 1

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,430
OFFICER:

3
00:00:03,430 --> 00:00:04,037
Good morning.

4
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:06,000
What can I do for you?

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,050
LOUISE:

6
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:08,471
I want to report a theft.

7
00:00:08,471 --> 00:00:12,000
I had some things stolen out of my bag yesterday.

8
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,389
OFFICER:

9
00:00:12,389 --> 00:00:14,334
I'm sorry to hear that.

10
00:00:14,334 --> 00:00:14,723
Right,

11
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:17,836
so I'll need to take a few details.

12
00:00:17,836 --> 00:00:20,170
Can I start with your name?

13
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:20,987
LOUISE:

14
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:22,620
Louise Taylor.

15
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:23,065
OFFICER:

16
00:00:23,065 --> 00:00:24,398
OK, thank you.

17
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:27,510
And are you resident in the UK?

18
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:28,017
LOUISE:

19
00:00:28,017 --> 00:00:32,580
No, I'm actually Canadian, though my mother was British.

20
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:32,993
OFFICER:

21
00:00:32,993 --> 00:00:35,060
And your date of birth?

22
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,165
LOUISE:

23
00:00:36,165 --> 00:00:39,480
December 14th, 1977.

24
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:39,983
OFFICER:

25
00:00:39,983 --> 00:00:43,000
So you're just visiting this country?

26
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,408
LOUISE:

27
00:00:43,408 --> 00:00:44,225
That's right.

28
00:00:44,225 --> 00:00:47,084
I come over most summers on business.

29
00:00:47,084 --> 00:00:52,802
I'm an interior designer and I come over to buy old furniture, antiques you

30
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:53,210
know.

31
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,889
There are some really lovely things around here,

32
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:59,237
but you need to get out to the small towns.

33
00:00:59,237 --> 00:01:02,920
I've had a really good trip this year, until this happened.

34
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:03,373
OFFICER:

35
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:03,827
OK.

36
00:01:03,827 --> 00:01:07,000
So you've been here quite a while?

37
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,434
LOUISE:

38
00:01:07,434 --> 00:01:10,039
Yes, I'm here for two months.

39
00:01:10,039 --> 00:01:12,210
I go back next week.

40
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:12,613
OFFICER:

41
00:01:12,613 --> 00:01:15,840
So may I ask where you're staying now?

42
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,284
LOUISE:

43
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:20,724
Well at present I've got a place at Park Apartments,

44
00:01:20,724 --> 00:01:22,500
that's on King Street.

45
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,625
I was staying at the Riverside Apartments on the same street,

46
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:30,375
but the apartment there was only available for six weeks

47
00:01:30,375 --> 00:01:33,000
so I had to find another one.

48
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:33,578
OFFICER:

49
00:01:33,578 --> 00:01:34,157
OK.

50
00:01:34,157 --> 00:01:36,470
And the apartment number?

51
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:37,520
LOUISE:

52
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:38,570
Fifteen.

53
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:39,395
OFFICER:

54
00:01:39,395 --> 00:01:40,220
Right.

55
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:40,610
OFFICER:

56
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:44,510
Now, I need to take some details of the theft.

57
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:49,190
So you said you had some things stolen out of your bag?

58
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:49,833
LOUISE:

59
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:51,120
That's right.

60
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:51,546
OFFICER:

61
00:01:51,546 --> 00:01:56,660
And were you actually carrying the bag when the theft took place?

62
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:57,080
Yes.

63
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,180
I really can't understand it.

64
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:01,280
I had my backpack on.

65
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:05,900
And I went into a supermarket to buy a few things

66
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:10,100
and when I opened it up my wallet wasn't there.

67
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:10,533
OFFICER:

68
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:14,000
And what did your wallet have in it?

69
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,407
LOUISE:

70
00:02:14,407 --> 00:02:19,695
Well, fortunately I don't keep my credit cards in that wallet - I keep

71
00:02:19,695 --> 00:02:24,170
them with my passport in an inside compartment in my backpack.

72
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:31,637
But there was quite a bit of cash there...about ￡250 sterling, I should

73
00:02:31,637 --> 00:02:32,170
think.

74
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:35,422
I withdrew ￡300 from my account yesterday,

75
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:38,674
but I did a bit of shopping,

76
00:02:38,674 --> 00:02:43,320
so I must have already spent about ￡50 of that.

77
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,245
OFFICER:

78
00:02:44,245 --> 00:02:45,170
OK.

79
00:02:45,170 --> 00:02:45,534
LOUISE:

80
00:02:45,534 --> 00:02:50,628
At first I thought, oh I must have left the wallet back in the

81
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:50,992
apartment,

82
00:02:50,992 --> 00:02:54,630
but then I realised my phone had gone as well.

83
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:56,993
It was only a week old,

84
00:02:56,993 --> 00:03:00,144
and that's when I realised I'd been robbed.

85
00:03:00,144 --> 00:03:04,870
Anyway at least they didn't take the keys to my rental car.

86
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:05,463
OFFICER:

87
00:03:05,463 --> 00:03:06,057
Yes.

88
00:03:06,057 --> 00:03:10,210
So you say the theft occurred yesterday?

89
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,105
LOUISE:

90
00:03:11,105 --> 00:03:12,000
Yes.

91
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,430
OFFICER:

92
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:15,007
So that was September the tenth.

93
00:03:15,007 --> 00:03:19,303
And do you have any idea at all of where

94
00:03:19,303 --> 00:03:23,170
or when the things might possibly have been stolen?

95
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:23,537
LOUISE:

96
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:28,676
Well at first I couldn't believe it because the bag had been on my

97
00:03:28,676 --> 00:03:31,980
back ever since I left the apartment after lunch.

98
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:34,002
It's just a small backpack,

99
00:03:34,002 --> 00:03:39,662
but I generally use it when I'm travelling because it seems safer than a

100
00:03:39,662 --> 00:03:40,066
handbag.

101
00:03:40,066 --> 00:03:42,897
Anyway, I met up with a friend,

102
00:03:42,897 --> 00:03:46,940
and we spent a couple of hours in the museum.

103
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:52,242
But I do remember that as we were leaving there, at about 4 o'clock,

104
00:03:52,242 --> 00:03:55,651
a group of young boys ran up to us,

105
00:03:55,651 --> 00:03:58,302
and they were really crowding round us,

106
00:03:58,302 --> 00:04:03,604
and they were asking us what time it was, then all of a sudden

107
00:04:03,604 --> 00:04:04,740
they ran off.

108
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:05,269
OFFICER:

109
00:04:05,269 --> 00:04:08,440
Can you remember anything about them?

110
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:08,965
LOUISE:

111
00:04:08,965 --> 00:04:16,322
The one who did most of the talking was wearing a T-shirt with a

112
00:04:16,322 --> 00:04:18,949
picture of something...let's see...

113
00:04:18,949 --> 00:04:20,000
a tiger.

114
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:20,398
OFFICER:

115
00:04:20,398 --> 00:04:20,796
Right.

116
00:04:20,796 --> 00:04:24,380
Any idea of how old he might have been?

117
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:25,080
LOUISE:

118
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,880
Around twelve years old?

119
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,366
OFFICER:

120
00:04:28,366 --> 00:04:32,740
And can you remember anything else about his appearance?

121
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,436
LOUISE:

122
00:04:33,436 --> 00:04:34,827
Not much.

123
00:04:34,827 --> 00:04:37,610
He was quite thin...

124
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,148
OFFICER:

125
00:04:38,148 --> 00:04:39,760
Colour of hair?

126
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,265
LOUISE:

127
00:04:40,265 --> 00:04:43,803
I do remember that - he was blond.

128
00:04:43,803 --> 00:04:46,330
All the others were dark-haired.

129
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:46,840
OFFICER:

130
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:49,900
And any details of the others?

131
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,481
LOUISE:

132
00:04:50,481 --> 00:04:51,643
Not really.

133
00:04:51,643 --> 00:04:55,130
They came and went so quickly.

134
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:55,579
OFFICER:

135
00:04:55,579 --> 00:04:56,027
Right.

136
00:04:56,027 --> 00:05:02,309
So what I'm going to do now is give you a crime reference number

137
00:05:02,309 --> 00:05:05,450
so you can contact your insurance company.

138
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:12,814
So this is ten digits:

139
00:05:12,814 --> 00:05:15,760
87954 82361

140
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,525
LOUISE:

141
00:05:16,525 --> 00:05:18,055
Thank you.

142
00:05:18,055 --> 00:05:20,350
So should I ...
